1. She has a fear of disappointing her audience. (Verbatim: "I live in permanent fear of disappointing people.")
2. She recently returned from a trip to Japan. (Verbatim: "I've been in Japan like and I was so upset over the Xbox mic thing.")
3. She experienced technical difficulties with her Xbox microphone, which prevented her from streaming. (Verbatim: "It literally killed me inside for that microphone.")
4. She refers to herself as a "workaholic goose" and has adopted the "goose" persona. (Verbatim: "workaholic goose naughty goose workaholic though perhaps perhaps.")
5. She enjoys creating and organizing her streaming schedule and thumbnails in advance. (Verbatim: "I made my schedule and then I made all the thumbnails for the week.")
6. She uses the VData schedule page and values its layout for organizing streams. (Verbatim: "I really do like the vdata schedule page... it's really nice.")
7. She has a habit of staying up late to prepare for streams, sometimes working on thumbnails until 3–4 a.m. (Verbatim: "That was like 3-4 a.m. Wait, you know the exact time I posted my waiting rooms? What's it? Like, 3:30 a.m.")
8. She often sleeps in short chunks, typically around 3–5 hours, due to her streaming schedule. (Verbatim: "Most of my sleep has been in like three, four hour chunks.")
9. She consumes chocolate brownies and chocolate yogurt for breakfast. (Verbatim: "I had a chocolate yogurt and a chocolate brownie and a glass of water.")
10. She relies on caffeine and content creation over sleep, indicating a possible dependency or habit. (Verbatim: "All I need is caffeine. Yeah. Yeah.") [end of text]



1. Her full name includes "Stellaria" as her middle name. (Verbatim: "i went satsu stellaria that is my middle name")

2. She is from England and speaks with a natural West Country/farmer-like accent. (Verbatim: "if i was to go fully natural i would speak in a farmer farmer like a farmer like accent")

3. She finds doing accents very difficult and can only naturally do her own RP and West Country accent. (Verbatim: "i find accents very very very very difficult to do like it i've got the rp accent")

4. She lived in student halls in England and had to use laundrettes, which she disliked due to having to carry laundry. (Verbatim: "one of the student halls i lived in had to go to the laundrette but it was like not too far but it sucked because you have to like carry your laundry with you")

5. She has a strong desire to move to Japan in the future. (Verbatim: "i will literally move to japan help me i will literally move i just don't know how")

6. She struggles with a sense of direction and frequently gets lost, even when trying not to. (Verbatim: "boom lost every heckin time like i'm so confused like")

7. She wants to become a voice actress and believes it would be fun, though she doesn’t know how to get into the industry. (Verbatim: "i would love to be a va artist i would love to be a va like i don't know how to get into it")

8. She refers to her streaming schedule as including a morning and evening stream 12 hours apart to accommodate time zones. (Verbatim: "my typical streaming schedule is a stream at this time and a stream like literally 12 hours later")

9. She mentions enjoying streaming more than creating other types of content, despite knowing she should diversify. (Verbatim: "i enjoy streaming like a lot as you can tell from my utter addiction to it")

10. She used to live in student housing in England and considers herself lucky to not have relied on laundrettes often. (Verbatim: "i was always really lucky i never actually had to no no no actually one of my one of the student halls i lived in had to go to the laundrette") [end of text]



1. She has a recurring tendency to get lost and lead people to dead ends, which she humorously refers to as "the Elia Stellaria experience." (Verbatim: "that is the ellia stellaria experience like that is that is the ellia stellaria experience if i ever show anyone around anywhere i will lead them to a dead end")

2. She participated in a collab playing a game called *Content Warning*, where she got lost while trying to return to the ship after her teammates died. (Verbatim: "so i did a collab playing um what's it called content content warning and um and there was one part where everyone had died but me and i was trying to get myself back to the to the little ship in the game and i got lost")

3. Despite panicking during scary games, she claims to be calm and collected, joking that she lies about it. (Verbatim: "no panic no panic i never panic you know slap me in a job interview and i can talk about how i'm so calm and collected under pressure")

4. She has experience with job interviews and describes herself as calm under pressure, using corporate jargon effectively. (Verbatim: "i can deal with high pressure environments and work very well in stressful situations i do not panic and i'm calm collected")

5. She is skilled at writing CVs/resumes and transforming any experience into a professional strength using corporate language. (Verbatim: "i've been told i'm very good at writing cvs or i guess you guys call them resumes like i got it down i can take any heckin thing and be like yep let's make that a skill")

6. Her early streaming days were terrifying and filled with doubt, but she pushed through despite being nervous. (Verbatim: "i remember first few streams that i did were terrifying... it's so full of doubt you know like it's terrifying to hit that go live button because you are putting yourself out there")

7. She believes in taking risks and stepping outside her comfort zone to avoid future regrets, influenced by her parents often talking about regret. (Verbatim: "i don't want to look back with any regrets... i think that's because i had parents that were constantly constantly constantly talking about regret")

8. She views life as a game where facing high-risk challenges yields greater growth ("xp"), even if failure leads to lasting embarrassment. (Verbatim: "if life was a game you know just hit myself with those high xp bosses")

9. She goes through phases of low productivity where she spends entire days in bed, but eventually boredom turns into motivation. (Verbatim: "there's days where i'm like a complete potato and i just spend the whole day in bed doing nothing... i allow myself to get nothing done")

10. She feels constant pressure to be productive, possibly due to her upbringing, and struggles with feeling like she needs to do more because time passes quickly. (Verbatim: "i feel like maybe it's just the way i was raised or something where or my drive i don't know like yeah where it just feels like i always need to do more") [end of text]



1. She went to Japan on holiday and had family issues during that time. (Verbatim: "I went to Japan. Yeah. I went on holiday. And I had some family issues.")
2. She is considering or expressing a desire to move back to Japan permanently. (Verbatim: "She went on holiday and now she wants to go back permanently.")
3. She finds chess mentally exhausting and it leaves her very tired. (Verbatim: "But they always took out so much brain power. That made me so tired in EB.")
4. She is not very good at chess despite understanding the rules. (Verbatim: "I do understand chess. I'm not very good at it.")
5. She believes the best revenge is personal success and advocates for kindness. (Verbatim: "Revenge is the best revenge is your own success right? So yeah... Gotta be kind.")
6. She identifies as lazy and too tired to carry hate or be bothered with anger. (Verbatim: "I'm too lazy to be hateful. I'm literally too lazy to be bothered to be angry.")
7. She has a personal motto or rule: "Rule zero: be kind." (Verbatim: "rule zero be kind")
8. She used to host morning streams, attempting to stream right after waking up. (Verbatim: "I used to have it as a first thing, a morning stream as well.")
9. She is working on improving her speed reading skills. (Verbatim: "I'm working on my speed reading skills. I'm working on it.")
10. She denies being a bot and affirms her identity as a real person. (Verbatim: "It's not a bot, it's me. Hi, it's me, not a bot, I'm a real girl.") [end of text]



1. Elia Stellaria officially debuted as a VTuber around the middle of April, about a year before the stream. (Verbatim: "it's been a year since i became ellie... in april... middle of april")

2. She prepared her debut in only six days, which was an extremely stressful and intense period for her. (Verbatim: "i had six days to prep a mini debut... it took six days... it was a very very stressful time")

3. No one believed she created everything in six days, but she has proof and insists it's true. (Verbatim: "people didn't actually believe that that it took six days but it truly did like i have all the receipts")

4. She identifies as a professional procrastinator and thrives under pressure. (Verbatim: "i'm a professional procrastinator so you know being a professional procrastinator it really i am truly in my element when i am drowning in pressure")

5. She experienced a lot of emotional difficulty during her debut period, including crying and pain. (Verbatim: "i remember a lot of crying and a lot of pain yeah yeah")

6. She has considered doing a stream revisiting her temporary debut form. (Verbatim: "maybe we should do a stream where i'm back in my temporary form and revisit myself")

7. She values her viewers' well-being over their presence in streams and never wants them to feel guilty for being away. (Verbatim: "the main thing i want is for you to be looking after yourself... i would never be mad at someone for not being here")

8. She finds comfort in being relaxing to listen to and aims to make people smile. (Verbatim: "i'm very relaxing to listen to oh i'm glad i'm glad i could be of some comfort")

9. She expresses a desire to become a marketable plushie and jokes about fans eating her. (Verbatim: "i should make a plushie... please do not eat it... actually no screw it you can eat it")

10. She does not consider herself a goose, despite being called one by fans. (Verbatim: "i'm not a goose i'm not a goose i'm not a goose") [end of text]



1. She struggled with making friends during school and did not have friends then. (Verbatim: "yeah i didn't have i didn't have friends in school so being able to have such wonderful friends...")

2. She has social anxiety, which makes social interactions difficult for her. (Verbatim: "i'm an person you know i have awful awful social anxiety and whatnot and that's okay")

